  {
    "id": "jose_ex2_note",
    "type": "comment",
    "z": "jose_ex2_tab",
    "name": "Setup: paste a 32-byte secret into the key configuration first",
    "info": "1. Generate a random 32-byte secret: `openssl rand -base64 32`\n2. Open the *demo A256GCM secret* configuration (menu > Configuration nodes, or double-click the encrypt node and edit its key), keep *Use for* on **Encryption (JWE)** and paste the secret into **Secret**. Encoding stays `base64`; direct encryption needs exactly 32 bytes.\n3. Deploy, then click the inject button.\n\nExpected debug output: the compact JWE (five dot-separated parts, header `alg: dir`, `enc: A256GCM`), then the decrypted claims `{ sub: \"alice\", role: \"admin\", aud: \"example-service\", iat, exp }`.\n\nA token encrypted under another secret, a tampered token or an expired one goes to the *rejected* output with `msg.error.code` set and without any decrypted claims.\n\nThe decrypt node accepts audience `example-service`; changing the injected aud claim makes it reject the token.",
    "x": 250,
    "y": 40,
    "wires": []
  },
  {
    "id": "jose_ex2_inject",
    "type": "inject",
    "z": "jose_ex2_tab",
    "name": "claims",
    "props": [
      {
        "p": "payload"
      }
    ],
    "repeat": "",
    "crontab": "",
    "once": false,
    "onceDelay": 0.1,
    "topic": "",
    "payload": "{\"sub\":\"alice\",\"role\":\"admin\",\"aud\":\"example-service\"}",
    "payloadType": "json",
    "x": 130,
    "y": 120,
    "wires": [["jose_ex2_encrypt"]]
  },
  {
    "id": "jose_ex2_encrypt",
    "type": "jose-encrypt",
    "z": "jose_ex2_tab",
    "name": "",
    "key": "jose_ex2_key",
    "claims": "payload",
    "claimsType": "msg",
    "typ": "JWT",
    "expiryMode": "ttl",
    "ttlSeconds": 3600,
    "expiresAt": "",
    "issuedAt": true,
    "notBeforeMode": "preserve",
    "notBeforeSeconds": 0,
    "notBeforeAt": "",
    "tokenTo": "payload",
    "tokenToType": "msg",
    "x": 300,
    "y": 120,
    "wires": [["jose_ex2_token", "jose_ex2_decrypt"]]
  },
